<%# max-w-2xl, which is what every other form page in the app uses. This was `lg:w-2/3`, a
    *fraction* of the viewport - on a 1920px monitor that is a 1280px-wide single-column form, with a
    name field stretched across all of it. A form's measure does not scale with the window. %>
<%# "You can add students once it exists" was reported as unhelpful, and it was: adding students is the
    obvious next step and the classroom page offers it, so the sentence spent itself on the one thing the
    reader would have found anyway.

    `after_create :create_gradebooks_for_quarters` is the part nobody would guess - four grade books appear,
    one per quarter of the school year - and it is consequence-shaped like the sibling pages' descriptions
    ("They can sign in as soon as you save", "Changes apply everywhere this student appears").

    Held in a local because a comment tag cannot sit inside the render tag's argument list. I have now made
    that mistake four times; `test/views/no_nested_erb_tags_test.rb` caught this one in 30ms, which is what it
    is for. %>
<% description = "Creating it adds a grade book for each quarter of the school year." %>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "New classroom",
                       description: description } do %><% end %>

  <%= render "form", classroom: @classroom %>
</div>
